From 1c6c681d742093d3c9059cc0d43a1efb35aaf252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:28:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] backends/color: Encode built-in native SDR over a declared
 physical range

On a built-in panel in the native SDR mode, a declared target peak above
203 cd/m2 selects a native-gamma HDR route: the output stays gamma 2.2
over its base EDID primaries, but its encoding spans the declared physical
range, with SDR white at 203 cd/m2 times the reference factor, kept
strictly between the declared black and peak, and the same range as the
luminance target. The reference-white backlight holds the sysfs backlight
at maximum, so the declared peak stays the full-backlight peak.

Without a declared peak, and on external monitors, the native SDR mode is
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BCWL9z1ijNdgVDMvuiX96f
---
